%richness of the theory, which we take as a sign of naturality of our construction. Of particular interest is the large number of finite types, which greatly exceeds 
%the number of finite types of cluster algebras of the same rank. For example, in the sequel \cite{LP2} we show that the number of finite types grows exponentially with rank.
