Let $S = \Z[\text{frozen variables}]$ be the polynomial ring generated by the variables associated to the non-internal regions.  Let $\FF = \Q(\text{all variables})$ be the rational function field in all the variables associated to internal or non-internal regions.
Let $t_{\W}$ be the initial seed with cluster variables corresponding to internal regions and exchange polynomials given by the rule above. Let $\A_{\W}$ be the LP algebra $t_{\W}$ generates.

\begin{example}
Consider the wiring diagram $\W$ shown in Figure \ref{fig:lp4}.  We have $$S = \Z[P,T,U,V,W,X,Y,Z]$$ and $\FF = \Frac(S[a,b,c])$.
 \begin{figure}[h!]
    \begin{center}
    \input{eLie223.pstex_t}
    \end{center}
    \caption{A wiring diagram $\W$ and the variable labels of its regions; the cluster complex of the corresponding normalized finite type LP algebra $\A_{\W}$.}
